    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are looking to capitalize on favorable matchups today, with **Yordan Alvarez** leading the charge at a 79.62 score. Despite facing a mid-tier arm in Luis Castillo, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in elite start, buoyed by a prime #2 lineup slot and an exceptional .451 xwOBA that maximizes his output in our Roto categories. **Junior Caminero** (72.80) and **Caleb Durbin** (70.78) provide excellent stability behind him; the latter benefits significantly from a 4.57 xERA matchup against Young, and while his aggressive base-running is slightly dampened by the opposing battery, his overall offensive floor remains high. We are also leaning into **Josh Smith** (61.73) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.03), both of whom receive significant positive adjustments due to their dynamic platoon advantages and projected stolen base opportunities, which are critical as we navigate a tight leaderboard.\n\nThe decision to bench **Pedro Ramirez** (37.39) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Pedro Ramirez** is a versatile switch-hitter, the matchup against Henderson presents a sub-optimal efficiency scenario that failed to clear our 40-point mandatory threshold for active starts, especially when compared to the superior volume expectations for **Jacob Gonzalez** and **Chase Meidroth**. We are monitoring the status of **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** closely, as his 66.03 rating is heavily reliant on a favorable park factor and a slow opposing delivery that should invite high-percentage stolen base attempts. We remain cautious regarding **Jacob Gonzalez** (45.43) and **Chase Meidroth** (47.26); their lower-third lineup placement limits their R/RBI potential, and they are essentially serving as placeholders until **Trea Turner**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, or **Colt Keith** return to active schedules. With no weather threats currently flagged, we are prioritizing high-OPS contributors like **Christian Yelich** to ensure we maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 aggregate.",
